  "course_description": "Spring. Multidisciplinary in nature, the readings of the senior seminar reflect the centrality of the historical and cultural contributions of African Americans to American history and culture.",
  "course_notes": "(Same as HIST 496 1) (Complete Topic - Lights, Camera, Action! : Black Life and Culture in HBO's The Gilded Age) (This course will explore history, culture, and storytelling through the medium of television. We will examine the history of Black America from 1865 through the 1890s via the backdrop of HBO's hit television show \"The Gilded Age.\" Required for AAS Majors in Senior Year. Open to AAS Minors and seniors across ECAS.)",
